        "problem": "Find the inverse Laplace transform for $F(s)=\\frac{3}{2s-4}.$",
        "worked_solution": "From the table of Laplace transforms, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{2t}} & =\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{s-2}=\\frac{3}{2s-4},\\,s>2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{2t}} & =\\frac{3}{2s-4} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{L{\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{2t}}} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{3}{2s-4}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}{e}^{2t} & ={L}^{-1}{\\frac{3}{2s-4}} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{3}{2s-4}} & =\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{2t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
